/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (-Sliding Window \(3 seconds\): The microphone continuously records audio, updating the buffer every second. Features are extracted and predictions are made based on the latest three seconds of speech.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (-Audio Processing & Feature Extraction: Audio is RMS-normalized and processed using Librosa to extract MFCCs \(n=40\), chromagram, spectral centroid, and spectral bandwidth. Features are transformed into a 2D format for CNN inference.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (-Continuous Predictions: If fewer than three seconds of data are available, zero-padding is applied. Once the buffer is filled, predictions are updated every second.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
